# The repository holds code and installers. It never holds a machine's state, a credential, or a build artefact.
#
# This file is a backstop for the repository root. The program tree carries its own, stricter boundary at
# athena-agent/.gitignore — that is the one that matters, because that is where an installation's state would land
# if someone ever ran the agent from a clone instead of from ~/.athena.

# generated bytecode — a .pyc embeds the absolute path it was compiled from
*.py[co]
__pycache__/

# a local environment, if someone builds one in place
.venv/

# databases and session files
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.session

# editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
